# Reviewed readers of a tree of ci/job-rules that ci/jobselect cannot map to jobs by itself (a .go file maps by its package; a line of ci.yml by its job;
# a recipe line of the Makefile by the ci.yml jobs that call its target; another workflow by none). Tab-separated:
# <tree/>	<file>	<number of lines>	<text the lines contain, or *>	<jobs that run the file, comma-separated, or ->	<reason>
# Exactly that many lines of the file must name the tree and contain the text: a new line, a changed one or a missing one makes the tree select every job
# (and ci/jobselect check fails), so a new reader is always reviewed.
ci/kind/	loadtest/kind/run.sh	1	ci/kind/smoke/wd-lib.sh	-	the kind load test sources the kind lane's helpers; run only by make load-kind (no ci.yml job calls it: a recipe line of load-kind maps to no job)
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/charts.sh	1	deploy/helm/qv-business	-	the kind lane installs the charts; ci/kind scripts run only from make kind-* and kind.yml (the ci/kind tree has no ci.yml reader: jobselect readers)
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/install.sh	1	deploy/helm/qv-certs	-	same: the kind lane
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/parties.sh	1	deploy/helm/qv-party	-	same: the kind lane
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/signing.sh	2	deploy/helm/qv-	-	same: the kind lane
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/smoke/upgrade.sh	1	chart=deploy/helm/qv-business	-	same: the kind lane
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/teesim.sh	2	deploy/helm/qv-	-	same: the kind lane
deploy/helm/	deploy/cloud/aws/values/render_test.py	1	repo / "deploy/helm"	-	renders the charts with helm template; run only by deploy/cloud/aws/check.sh in .github/workflows/terraform.yml
loadtest/	Makefile	1	SCENARIO ?= loadtest/scenarios/smoke.json	e2e-evm-4	the default scenario of load-local, which load-smoke (the e2e-evm-4 job) calls
loadtest/	Makefile	1	KIND_SCENARIO := loadtest/scenarios/evm-kind.json	-	used only by the recipe of load-kind, which no ci.yml job calls
monitoring/	ci/promtool-tests.sh	2	monitoring	checks	promtool and the Go rule tests; run by the checks job (ci.yml, through ci/run-groups.sh)
monitoring/	docker-compose.yml	2	profiles: ["monitoring"]	-	the compose profile's name, not a path
monitoring/	docker-compose.yml	1	./monitoring:/etc/prometheus:ro	-	the dev Prometheus (profile monitoring, make monitoring-up); ci/infra.sh never starts it (it names its services; the profile is not one of them)
loadtest/	ci/e2e-prebuild.sh	1	./loadtest/cmd/qv-load	e2e-evm-1,e2e-evm-2,e2e-evm-3,e2e-evm-4	the build job compiles the load generator for the e2e/custody jobs (they start it); its Go package is in their graph too
deploy/helm/	ci/kind/check-pins.sh	2	deploy/helm/*/values-kind*.yaml	-	the kind lane's image pin check reads the values-kind files; run only by .github/workflows/helm.yml (and by hand), which runs on deploy/helm/** and ci/kind/**
